`stopLoading` fires `REDISMODULE_SUBEVENT_LOADING_ENDED` or `LOADING_FAILED` depending on its argument. The PR didn't add the new success code there:

::code{file="src/aof.c" lines="1893-1895"}

When the last file is recovered, `ret == AOF_BROKEN_RECOVERED`, so modules get `LOADING_FAILED` even though the dataset loaded and the server keeps running. Modules that react to load failure, for example by resetting their own state, will do the wrong thing.

